<%# One row of the Ranked view.

    The row is mobile-first: DOM order IS the phone layout, and `sm:order-*`
    restores the desktop reading order (rank, status, title, root, menu) above
    640px. At phone width the row is two lines —

      ⠿  Some session title that wraps to two lines           ⋮
         Rank [ 1000 ]  Needs input

    — because a single line at 375px leaves the title about eighty pixels, which
    is not a title. The meta group is `w-full` below `sm:`, which is what forces
    the wrap deterministically rather than hoping the content overflows.

    Locals:
      agent_session  - the session
      draggable_row  - true for spot rows (draggable, editable precedence),
                       false for priority rows (no rank to order by) %>
<li class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1.5 px-3 py-2 text-sm sm:flex-nowrap sm:gap-x-3 <%= "cursor-grab" if draggable_row %>"
    id="ranked_row_<%= agent_session.id %>"
    data-ranked-queue-target="row"
    data-session-id="<%= agent_session.id %>"
    data-precedence="<%= agent_session.precedence %>">
  <%# Rendered on every row, hidden on priority ones — see the note on the rank
      cell below: a row promoted or demoted swaps its controls in place.

      Padded into a touch target rather than sized as one: SortableJS only starts a
      drag from inside this box, and a 16px one on a phone is a box you miss. The
      padding rather than a `flex` box is deliberate — Tailwind emits `.inline-flex`
      AFTER `.hidden`, so a display utility here would beat the `hidden` that keeps
      the handle off priority rows, and every priority row would sprout a handle
      that drags nothing. %>
  <span class="shrink-0 px-1 py-2.5 text-gray-300 hover:text-gray-500 sm:order-1 sm:py-0 <%= "hidden" unless draggable_row %>"
        data-ranked-queue-target="handle" aria-hidden="true" title="Drag to reorder">
    <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M7 4a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm6 0a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zM7 9a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm6 0a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm-6 5a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2zm6 0a1 1 0 100 2 1 1 0 000-2z"/></svg>
  </span>

  <%# The title leads the row on a phone, because it is the only cell that tells
      you what the work is. Two clamped lines rather than one truncated one, and
      `break-words` because Zimmer titles are full of unbreakable tokens
      (`test_session_state_machine_transitions_...`) that would otherwise set the
      row's width. Desktop keeps the single truncated line it had. %>
  <%# A real <a href> whose plain left-click is intercepted by session-drawer#open,
      so the title opens the same right-side drawer the card grid's "View" opens
      rather than navigating off the queue. Middle-click, ⌘/Ctrl/Shift/Alt-click
      and "Open in new tab" are untouched — the controller returns without
      preventing the default for anything but an unmodified primary click, and
      below `sm` it declines entirely so a phone gets the full session page.

      The href is the full session page; session_drawer_url is the separate path
      the drawer's frame loads, so the frame never fetches a URL a link points at
      and no URL-keyed cache can serve it the frameless body. See
      SessionsController#drawer.

      turbo_prefetch: false is a cost measure, not a correctness one — an
      intercepted click never navigates to this href, so hover-prefetching the
      full page would always be wasted work. %>
  <%= link_to agent_session.title.presence || "Untitled session",
        session_path(agent_session),
        data: session_drawer_link_data(agent_session, turbo_prefetch: false),
        class: "min-w-0 flex-1 break-words font-medium text-gray-800 hover:text-indigo-600 max-sm:line-clamp-2 sm:order-3 sm:truncate" %>

  <%# Row actions behind a "⋮", the same overflow-menu controller the session card
      uses. Both entries are rendered on every row and one is hidden, for the same
      reason both rank cells are: a promote or a demote has to swap them in place.

      `headroom` is the vertical room the menu asks for beyond its own box before it
      gives up on opening downward. The card's menu opens a Pause Until panel inside
      itself and needs 400px of it; this menu opens nothing, so it asks for none —
      otherwise every row in the top two-thirds of the page would open upward. %>
  <div class="relative shrink-0 sm:order-5"
       data-controller="overflow-menu"
       data-overflow-menu-headroom-value="0"
       data-overflow-menu-placement-value="down">
    <button type="button"
            data-overflow-menu-target="button"
            data-action="overflow-menu#toggle"
            aria-haspopup="true"
            aria-expanded="false"
            title="More actions for session <%= agent_session.id %>"
            aria-label="More actions for session <%= agent_session.id %>"
            class="inline-flex h-9 w-9 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-gray-300 bg-white text-gray-500 hover:bg-gray-50 hover:text-gray-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-offset-1 focus:ring-indigo-500 sm:h-8 sm:w-8">
      <svg class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M10 6a1.5 1.5 0 110-3 1.5 1.5 0 010 3zM10 11.5a1.5 1.5 0 110-3 1.5 1.5 0 010 3zM10 17a1.5 1.5 0 110-3 1.5 1.5 0 010 3z" />
      </svg>
    </button>
    <div data-overflow-menu-target="menu"
         role="menu"
         class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full mt-2 z-30 w-56 max-w-[calc(100vw-2rem)] overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white py-1 shadow-lg">
      <button type="button"
              role="menuitem"
              data-ranked-queue-target="promoteAction"
              data-action="ranked-queue#promote overflow-menu#close"
              data-session-id="<%= agent_session.id %>"
              class="w-full px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50 <%= "hidden" unless draggable_row %>">Promote to priority</button>
      <button type="button"
              role="menuitem"
              data-ranked-queue-target="demoteAction"
              data-action="ranked-queue#demote overflow-menu#close"
              data-session-id="<%= agent_session.id %>"
              class="w-full px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50 <%= "hidden" if draggable_row %>">Demote to spot</button>
      <%# Start now: take this session's queued turn immediately rather than
          waiting out the gate's deferred re-check. Rendered on every row rather
          than only on the waiting ones, because the row is not re-rendered when a
          status arrives over the stream — only its status pill is — so a row
          hidden on render would stay hidden after the session went back to
          waiting, and one shown would stay shown. The action refuses a session
          that cannot start and says why. %>
      <%= link_to "Start now", start_now_session_path(agent_session),
            role: "menuitem",
            data: { turbo_method: :post, action: "overflow-menu#close" },
            class: "block w-full px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50" %>
      <%# A plain full-page navigation. turbo_prefetch: false is a cost measure and
          nothing more — /sessions/:id has exactly one body now, so warming it on
          hover could not poison the drawer even if it were left on; a ~900 KB page
          is simply not worth fetching on a hover over a menu item. %>
      <%= link_to "Open session", session_path(agent_session),
            role: "menuitem",
            data: { turbo_prefetch: false },
            class: "block w-full px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm text-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-50" %>
      <%# Trash posts to the same #archive action every other Trash affordance in
          the app posts to, so the queued-message speed bump and the Undo toast
          come along with it. The row itself leaves over the ranked stream — as a
          membership delivery the page judges, so it leaves a queue of live work
          and stays, reading "Trashed", on one filtered to show the trash. %>
      <%= link_to "Trash", archive_session_path(agent_session),
            role: "menuitem",
            data: { turbo_method: :post, action: "overflow-menu#close" },
            class: "block w-full border-t border-gray-100 px-4 py-2.5 text-left text-sm text-red-600 hover:bg-red-50" %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Rank and status travel together, and on a phone they take the second line —
      `w-full` is what puts them there. %>
  <div class="flex w-full min-w-0 items-center gap-2 sm:order-2 sm:w-auto sm:shrink-0">
    <span class="shrink-0 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-400 sm:hidden">Rank</span>

    <%# Precedence: editable inline for spot rows, greyed static text for priority
        ones so the number a demotion would land on is never a surprise.

        BOTH cells are rendered on every row and one of them is hidden. A promote or
        a demote moves the row between the two sections, and the controller swaps
        which cell is showing — so a demoted row is immediately draggable and
        editable, and shows its NEW rank, without waiting for a reload. %>
    <%= number_field_tag "precedence_#{agent_session.id}", agent_session.precedence,
          id: "precedence_input_#{agent_session.id}",
          disabled: !draggable_row,
          "aria-label": "Precedence for session #{agent_session.id}",
          data: { ranked_queue_target: "precedenceInput", action: "keydown.enter->ranked-queue#commitPrecedence blur->ranked-queue#revertUncommitted" },
          class: "w-24 shrink-0 rounded border border-gray-300 px-2 py-1.5 text-sm text-right tabular-nums focus:border-indigo-500 focus:ring-1 focus:ring-indigo-500 sm:py-1 #{'hidden' unless draggable_row}" %>
    <%# Auto-width on a phone so it reads as "RANK 40" rather than as a number
        marooned at the end of a column that only exists on a wider screen. %>
    <span class="shrink-0 text-right tabular-nums text-xs text-gray-400 sm:w-24 <%= "hidden" if draggable_row %>"
          data-ranked-queue-target="precedenceReadout"
          title="Precedence, unused while this session is priority"><%= agent_session.precedence %></span>

    <%= render "sessions/ranked_row_status", agent_session: agent_session %>
  </div>

  <span class="hidden shrink-0 text-xs text-gray-400 sm:order-4 sm:inline"><%= agent_session.agent_root_key.presence || agent_session.genesis_key %></span>
</li>
